5,1,1,talk,Rin,,Let's make this layout super smart! We shouldn't just guess where to sit. We need to look at the data first so we don't waste any time later. What should we check out?,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Toshio,,I agree. A data-driven approach is the most efficient way to avoid mistakes. We should prioritize the financial and physical constraints of the space before deciding on the actual arrangement.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,"I agree. However, we should also consider the human element. Let's ensure we look into the social dynamics and physical well-being of the team so the final arrangement is fair for everyone.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Shion,,"Logic is fine, but let's not forget the actual experience of sitting there. I'll take the sound meter readings across the room and the physio's note from the workstation check. Comfort is a non-negotiable variable.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Yumi,,"I'm so excited to get this right! I want us all to feel connected, so I'll look into what this year's two joiners reported and the drawn plan against the staff survey!","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Rin,,I want to know how we actually start our days! I'll check the morning routine on the pilot floor upstairs and the arrival times in the badge records. Let's see how we use our time!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"Since we need to be mindful of the budget, I will look into the basis of the department's floor billing and the facilities quote for re-running power and network. We must know the costs involved.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"To ensure we don't overlook any hidden tensions, I'll look into the unplanned seat shuffles in the past year and the two project strands within earshot last spring. We need to understand the history of this space.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Shion,,I've already claimed my two. I'll spend the rest of this round observing how you all justify your choices. It's more interesting to see what you prioritize than to do more work.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Yumi,,I've got mine covered too! I really think understanding how our new teammates felt and what everyone wants from the survey will help us stay close and happy. I can't wait to see what we find!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Rin,,Does everyone have their two things? I think we've covered everything from money to feelings! I'm really curious if the people upstairs have a secret trick for starting their mornings faster!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"It seems we have a comprehensive list. By dividing the research into financial, physical, and social categories, we can evaluate the options objectively. I look forward to seeing how the costs align with the team's needs.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Mizuki,,"It's a good start. By covering all these angles, we can avoid making a decision based on who speaks the loudest. I hope the data reveals any imbalances we need to address to keep things equitable.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Shion,,"It's a tidy distribution. Just ensure that when we review the results, we don't let ""social synergy"" override the physical reality of the workspace. A happy team is useless if they're in physical pain.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Yumi,,I totally agree with Shion! We need to be comfortable and happy at the same time. I'm just so glad we're all working together to make this a place where everyone feels welcome and connected!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Rin,,I'm all set! I can't wait to see the results. Let's make sure we really listen to what the data tells us so we can make the best choice for everyone!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
