65,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option A sounds like a nightmare! Imagine spending ten minutes every single morning just to get your screens working. We'd waste so much time! I definitely vote for Option C!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option A and B are financially unviable. The cost of constant rewiring and the inefficiency of shifting blocks would drain our budget. Option C is the only responsible choice as it ensures long-term stability.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Option C is the most stable, but it risks creating a permanent divide between those in prime spots and those in the worst. If we choose C, we must agree on how to handle that.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A and B are absurd. Forcing us to reset ergonomic adjustments daily or periodically is a recipe for physical strain and inefficiency. Option C is the only logical choice for anyone who values their health.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I agree with everyone! Option C is perfect because it gives us the stability we need while letting us group together by role. That way, we can keep supporting each other and helping new joiners grow!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Rin,,I'm so glad we all agree! Option C means no more morning cable scrambles and no wasted gaps in our day. It's the fastest and easiest way to get to work!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"It is the only option that aligns with our financial constraints. By eliminating recurring rewiring costs and maintaining a fixed footprint, we protect the budget while providing the stability the team requires.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"I can see that stability is the priority for everyone. While I still worry about the unfairness of permanent seating, I won't block the team's consensus. I'll support Option C, provided we are honest about the seat quality.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Shion,,"Finally, some common sense. Option C allows for the precise, long-term physical calibration required for actual productivity. Anything else is just a superficial attempt at ""fairness"" that ignores the reality of how our bodies work.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I'm just so happy we're all on the same page! Let's make sure we arrange those fixed groups so everyone feels included and the sunlight is shared as much as possible. I'm voting for Option C!,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm super happy we're all agreeing! No more wasting time on cables or rushing around. Option C is definitely the best for our schedules. I'm voting for C!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Toshio,,The consensus is clear. Option C is the only choice that prevents recurring financial waste and ensures the stability we need. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"Since the team's need for stability and physical health outweighs my concerns about rotation, I will align with the majority. I vote for Option C, but let's be mindful of the seat distribution.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Shion,,I've already made my position clear. Option C is the only choice that doesn't treat our physical well-being as an afterthought. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm so glad we're all looking out for each other! Let's make this a cozy and helpful space where everyone can shine. I vote for Option C!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Rin,,Yay! We did it! Everyone is happy and we save our time. I'm so excited to get started in our new spots! My final vote is Option C!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"The decision is logically sound and fiscally responsible. By choosing Option C, we secure the budget and ensure operational stability. My final vote is Option C.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,I'll support the team's consensus for the sake of stability and health. Let's just promise to be transparent about the seating quality when we finalize the map. My final vote is Option C.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Shion,,The result is inevitable. Option C is the only choice that respects the physical requirements of the workspace and the logic of efficiency. I vote for Option C.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I'm so happy we all agree! Let's make sure we set it up so we can all help each other and stay connected. My final vote is Option C!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
